{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:abcfd3a13438942b","name":"Remote Activation","source":{"id":"source:reference-abcfd3a13438942b","title":"Remote Activation","revision":19746,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:32:11Z","sha256":"c59c39eb4d2e77912b3b695553ba9864af59110c8a340fdf6ccbbe35020c2c43","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19746","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Remote%20Activation&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-abcfd3a13438942b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 100\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Upgrade Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Upgrade_Point"}," Cost:"]}," 0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["This Upgrade allows a piece of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," to be activated with a signal from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," or similar ",{"tag":"a","children":["Communications Device"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Communications_Device"},". Although typically associated with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosives"}," or security systems, Remote Activation can be used to set a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," to activate, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fusion Lantern"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fusion_Lantern","referenceId":"reference:c458f1ef779414e4"}," to flare to life, a computer to start running a program, or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holoprojector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holoprojector"}," to begin a recorded holoprojection. Activating a remote is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", which includes entering the special command code (allowing a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," to activate multiple pieces of Remote Activation gear, one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," per item activated).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The range of Remote Activation is determined by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," or other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Communications Device"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Communications_Device"}," used. Any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," can be used to activate the gear, sending a signal with a specific code along a specific frequency. A character aware of a piece of remotely activated gear can find the necessary frequency and activation code with a DC 30 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
